# Automatic releases (release-kit)

This repo is wired for **AI-assisted release engineering**. You (the agent) own the semver decision; Actions own merge/tag/release.

Do **not** ask the user to bump `package.json` or run a manual release.

## On every PR you open

1. Judge the **diff you implemented** (not the ticket title alone).
2. Set **exactly one** label via `gh pr create` / `gh pr edit`:

| Label | Use when | Bump |
|-------|----------|------|
| `release:major` | Breaking / incompatible behavior | `X.0.0` |
| `release:minor` | New user-facing capability | `x.Y.0` |
| `release:patch` | Fix, chore, docs, CI, refactor | `x.y.Z` |
| `release:skip` | No tag/release | — |

Default if unsure: **`release:patch`**.

```bash
gh pr create ... --label "release:minor"
```

3. Prefer PRs against the default branch. After one merges, Actions updates other open PRs onto trunk (strict up-to-date). Stacked PRs are OK — Actions retargets children after the base merges.

A `label-pr` workflow may auto-apply a label when none exists. **Your explicit label always wins.**
